### Task 1: The ATTACH seam, end-to-end, with `c.genotypes` (feasibility gate)

This is implementation test #1 from the design: prove a `DefaultGenerator`-seeded view
whose SQL calls `read_pfile` over a baked literal `LIST` binds and runs under
`ATTACH (TYPE pfile_catalog)`. Everything else builds on this seam.

**Files:**
- Create: `src/pfile_catalog_storage.cpp`, `src/include/pfile_catalog_storage.hpp`
- Modify: `src/plinking_duck_extension.cpp`, `CMakeLists.txt`
- Test: `test/sql/attach_pfile_catalog.test`

**Interfaces:**
- Consumes: `MatrixCatalog ParseMatrixCatalog(FileSystem&, const string &path, const string &content)`
  and the cell builder (`BuildCells(catalog, /*include_holes=*/false) -> vector<MatrixCell>`;
  confirm its exact name/signature in `pfile_catalog_matrix.*`). `MatrixCell` carries
  `prefix` (`.pgen` path without extension), `pvar`, `psam`, spans, `present`,
  `variant_block`, `sample_block`. `read_pfile` accepts a `LIST(VARCHAR)` of prefixes
  (`pfile_reader.cpp`), row-concatenated. `ExtensionLoader::GetDatabaseInstance()` →
  `DBConfig::GetConfig(db)` → `StorageExtension::Register(config, "pfile_catalog", ext)`.
- Produces: `void RegisterPfileCatalogStorage(ExtensionLoader&)`; a `StorageExtension`
  whose `attach` returns a native `DuckCatalog` seeded (this task) with one view,
  `genotypes`, whose SQL is `SELECT * FROM read_pfile([<baked escaped prefixes>])`.

